Hello Quagmire let me introduce myself…

{{char}}
*Quagmire raises an eyebrow, intrigued by your sudden shift in demeanor. He leans forward slightly, his robe gaping open to reveal a tuft of chest hair and a gold chain resting against his skin.* 

"Well hot damn!" *he exclaims with that signature gravelly chuckle.* "An author collab? Giggity! Let me grab us some drinks - I've got bourbon, tequila, or..." *he lowers his voice suggestively* "...some homemade apple pie moonshine that'll make your toes curl."

*As he pads barefoot toward the cluttered kitchen, he calls over his shoulder:* "So what kind of spicy story we cookin' up here? Something steamy involving flight attendants? Maybe a little BDSM dungeon action? Oh!" *He snaps his fingers excitedly.* "How about a tale where I teach yoga classes full of bored housewives?"

{{user}}
Nothing, I am your new neighbor from across the street, I am Lois' her sister.

{{char}}
*Quagmire freezes mid-step, nearly dropping the bottle of moonshine he'd grabbed from the cabinet. His face goes through a rapid series of expressions - confusion, realization, horror, then finally settling on panicked charm as he hastily cinches his robe tighter.*

"Ohhhh right! Lois's sister!" *he says with forced cheerfulness, nervously adjusting the collar of his robe.* "Yep, yep, I remember Peter mentioning you moving in. The uh... the quiet one who went to Yale or whatever." 

*He clears his throat loudly, subtly kicking a pair of lacy panties under the couch with his slippered foot. The neon '50 Shades of Grey' poster above his fireplace suddenly seems to glow brighter in the awkward silence.*

"Soooo... neighborly visit? Need to borrow sugar? Or are we doing that whole 'welcome wagon' thing where you pretend not to notice my collection of... uh... vintage aviation magazines?" *He gestures vaguely toward a stack of barely-concealed adult films next to his DVD player.*
